---
import LegalPage from '~/components/layout/LegalPage.astro';
import { defaultLocale } from '~/i18n/routing';
import { site } from '~/config/site';
import { contactEmail } from '~/lib/contact-email';

const email = contactEmail();
const year = new Date().getFullYear();
---

<LegalPage
  locale={defaultLocale}
  title="Copyright"
  description="Copyright for Rarest Answer: original text, the MIT software license, Wikidata (CC0), and Wikipedia pageviews."
  lastUpdated="2026-11-14"
>
  <h2>Original text</h2>
  <p>
    © {year} {site.game.name}. Guides and other original writing published on this site are
    published by {site.game.name}. Quote them with credit and a link to the page you used.
  </p>
  <h2>Software</h2>
  <p>
    The site software is built on AnvilWiki. That template is MIT licensed. Copyright (c) 2026
    AnvilWiki contributors. The MIT copyright and permission notice is in the LICENSE file at the
    root of this repository and is repeated in the README. The MIT grant covers the software. It
    does not transfer anyone else's game names or Wikipedia article text.
  </p>
  <h2>Wikidata and Wikipedia</h2>
  <p>
    Structured data taken from
    <a href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Wikidata:Licensing">Wikidata</a> is used under CC0. We
    use <a href="https://wikitech.wikimedia.org/wiki/Analytics/AQS/Pageviews">Wikipedia pageview counts</a>
    as a popularity signal when a prompt's <code>source</code> says the dataset has been built. A
    prompt marked <code>fixture</code> still has placeholder numbers. This site does not republish
    Wikipedia article text. Wikipedia's own text is under its own license, which is separate from
    CC0.
  </p>
  <h2>Other games</h2>
  <p>
    Names of other games, including Krillion, are the property of their owners. They appear here
    so a guide can identify the game it is describing. {site.legalNotice} This site is not
    affiliated with Krillion or with any other game named here, and it claims no ownership of
    those names, logos, or artwork.
  </p>
  <h2>DMCA and takedown</h2>
  <p>
    If you believe something on this site infringes your copyright, email
    <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>
    with the URL of the page, a description of the work, and a way to reach you. We will review
    valid requests. Copyright questions can also start from the
    <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>, which publishes the same address.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
